I built the sprint board in `/tmp/claude-0/runs/r15/board-react-opus-5/src/`: tabs in `App.tsx`, the board and detail in `Board.tsx`, the archive page in `Archive.tsx`, and the state logic in `board.ts`. `./check` passes and `./test` passes 26/26; the only console message was one 404 for a missing resource, probably the favicon. The board keeps what the server has confirmed plus a list of changes still waiting on it and always shows the two combined, so a declined change undoes only itself while other changes in flight stay on screen, and late replies from old column or checklist loads are ignored.

Choices the brief doesn't settle, which hidden tests might read differently:
- **Trimming:** titles and item text are trimmed before sending, and whitespace-only input does nothing.
- **Rename input:** `title-input` empties after a rename, like the other inputs.
- **Disabled moves:** `left`/`right` are disabled when the target column isn't loaded.
- **Cards being added:** a card waiting on `addCard` counts as nowhere to go for the `down` button of the card above it, and cards moved into To do go above it.
- **Extras:** the checklist and archive list have retry buttons, and an empty archive says "nothing archived".